{% if artifact.metadata and artifact.metadata.isWorkflow == true %}

## 0. Workflow Bootstrap

Before any shell command that may change the working directory, run the tracked workflow bootstrap tool:

```bash
rp1 agent-tools workflow-bootstrap \
  --name {{ artifact.workflowTarget.name }} \
  --schema-path {{ artifact.workflowTarget.schemaPath }} \
{% if artifact.metadata.arguments and artifact.metadata.arguments.size > 0 %}  --args "$ARGUMENTS" \
{% endif %}  --project-root "$PWD" \
  --harness {{ platform }}
```

Parse the JSON response. Extract values from `data.arguments`, `data.directories`, `data.workflow`, `data.run`, and `data.trace`:

| Variable | Source |
|----------|--------|
{%- if artifact.metadata.arguments and artifact.metadata.arguments.size > 0 %}
{%- for arg in artifact.metadata.arguments %}
| {{ arg.name }} | `data.arguments.{{ arg.name }}` |
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
| RUN_ID | `data.run.runId` |
| RUN_RESUMED | `data.run.resumed` |
| RUN_DECISION | `data.run.decision` |
| projectRoot | `data.directories.projectRoot` |
| kbRoot | `data.directories.kbRoot` |
| workRoot | `data.directories.workRoot` |
| rp1DirectoryStatus | `data.directories.status` |
| rp1NextStepCommand | `data.directories.nextStepCommand` |
| workflowName | `data.workflow.name` |
| workflowRunPolicy | `data.workflow.runPolicy` |
| requestedProjectRoot | `data.trace.requestedProjectRoot` |
| canonicalProjectRoot | `data.trace.canonicalProjectRoot` |

If workflow bootstrap fails, required arguments remain unresolved, or `rp1DirectoryStatus` is not `initialized`, warn the user about the tool error and stop.

Use `RUN_ID` for all subsequent emits and artifact registrations. Use the returned canonical directories for all subsequent paths. Do not call `resolve-args`, do not call `rp1-root-dir`, do not generate a UUID, and do not call `emit resume-run` directly.
{% elsif artifact.metadata and artifact.metadata.arguments and artifact.metadata.arguments.size > 0 %}

## 0. Resolve Arguments

Run the argument resolver to obtain all parameter values:

```bash
rp1 agent-tools resolve-args --name {{ namespacedPluginName }}:{{ artifact.name }} --args "$ARGUMENTS"
```

Parse the JSON response. Extract values from `data.arguments` and `data.directories`:

| Variable | Source |
|----------|--------|
{%- for arg in artifact.metadata.arguments %}
| {{ arg.name }} | `data.arguments.{{ arg.name }}` |
{%- endfor %}
| projectRoot | `data.directories.projectRoot` |
| kbRoot | `data.directories.kbRoot` |
| workRoot | `data.directories.workRoot` |
| rp1DirectoryStatus | `data.directories.status` |
| rp1NextStepCommand | `data.directories.nextStepCommand` |

If `data.unresolved` is non-empty, warn the user about missing required arguments and stop.

Use these resolved values for all subsequent steps. Do not call `rp1-root-dir`, re-derive project directories, or re-parse arguments.
{% endif %}

